# Arctic Wolves Video Companion Server
#
# ── Required ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   ENCRYPTION_KEY=<64-char hex string>
#
#   Generate with:  python -c "import os; print(os.urandom(32).hex())"
#
#   This key encrypts the config file on the persistent Docker volume.
#   Use the same key as the main app if you want matching PII encryption.
#   Set it in docker-compose.yml or pass it via your orchestrator.
#
# ── Setup flow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. Set ENCRYPTION_KEY in docker-compose.yml or environment.
#   2. Start the container:  docker compose up -d
#   3. Visit http://localhost:5100 — the setup page will appear.
#   4. Create an admin account (username + password).
#   5. Configure S3/RustFS credentials (or push them from the main app later).
#   6. Click "Generate API Key" — copy the key.
#   7. Enter the generated key in the main app's Game Plan Settings →
#      Companion Server → API Key.
#
# All other configuration (API key, RustFS credentials, hardware acceleration,
# admin account) is managed through the companion web UI and stored in an
# AES-256-CBC encrypted config file on the persistent Docker volume.
#
# If the container is updated, the encrypted config persists on the volume.
# If the volume is lost, the setup page will appear again on first start.
#
# Storage paths (where videos live, where HLS output goes) are controlled
# entirely by the main application — it tells the companion exactly where
# each source file is and where to write the transcoded output.
